# 📦 TryHackMe – Packets & Frames

## 📌 Overview
This room explores how data is transmitted across computer networks using packets and frames. It introduces the fundamentals of network communication and explains how data travels between devices.

## 🎯 What I Learned

- **Packets:** Understanding how data is divided into smaller units for transmission across networks.
- **Frames:** Learning how packets are encapsulated into frames at the Data Link Layer.
- **OSI Model:** Understanding the role of network layers in data communication.
- **TCP/IP:** Exploring how devices communicate using the TCP/IP protocol suite.
- **Encapsulation:** Understanding how data gets wrapped with headers and other information at different network layers.
- **Network Communication:** Learning how devices send and receive data across a network.

## 🔍 Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---|---|
| Packet | A unit of data at the Network Layer |
| Frame | A unit of data at the Data Link Layer |
| IP Address | Identifies a device on a network |
| MAC Address | Identifies a network interface |
| Encapsulation | Wrapping data with protocol information |
| Decapsulation | Removing protocol information at the receiving end |

## 🛠️ Skills Practiced
- Networking Fundamentals
- OSI Model
- TCP/IP Protocol Suite
- Data Encapsulation
- Packet and Frame Analysis
- Network Communication

